cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "disegreg: shared analysis of solute segregation and defect phases at dislocations in atomistic simulations"
abstract: >-
  disegreg analyses LAMMPS molecular-dynamics / Monte-Carlo snapshots of
  single dislocations in fcc alloys with one common, versioned set of
  definitions. Version 0.1 covers one run at a time: dislocation lines
  (OVITO DXA) with exact periodic distances in triclinic cells and a
  structural fallback where DXA misses the line, region-resolved solute
  concentrations, the line excess Gamma(R), chemical short-range order,
  solute clusters, drift tests and block-averaged time averages, plus a tidy
  results table across runs. Cross-run diagnostics (uptake exponent, McLean
  comparison, bulk-control and hysteresis comparisons) are planned for
  version 0.2.
  Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research
  Foundation) through Project No. A02 of the SFB 1394 "Structural and
  Chemical Atomic Complexity – From Defect Phase Diagrams to Material
  Properties", Project ID 409476157.
